{"name":"Iris Bloom","hex":"#5b649e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"iris","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the genus Iris, common in the northern hemisphere, and generally having attractive blooms (See  Iris (plant) on  Wikipedia.Wikipedia ).","The contractile membrane perforated by the pupil, which adjusts to control the amount of light reaching the retina, and which forms the colored portion of the eye (See  Iris (anatomy) on  Wikipedia.Wikipedia )."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To open or close in the manner of an iris.","To cause (something) to shine with the colours of the rainbow; to make iridescent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iris"},{"term":"bloom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A blossom; the flower of a plant; an expanded bud.","Flowers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause to blossom; to make flourish.","To bestow a bloom upon; to make blooming or radiant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bloom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iris (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is a flowering plant genus of 320 accepted species with showy flowers. As well as being the scientific name, iris is also widely used as a common name for all Iris species, as well as some belonging to other closely related genera. A common name for some species is flags, while the plants of the subgenus Scorpiris are widely known as junos, particularly in horticulture. It is a popular garden flower."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(plant)","wikidata":"Q156901"},{"title":"Iris (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is an ambiguous color term, usually referring to shades ranging from blue-violet to violet."}],"image":"https: